<title>CANADA: Canada to auction C$1.3 billion bonds due 2027.</title>
<headline>Canada to auction C$1.3 billion bonds due 2027.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Government of Canada said it plans to auction on January 22 C$1.3 billion of bonds with a coupon of 8.00 percent and maturing on June 1, 2027.</p>
<p>The Bank of Canada said it will buy at least C$195 million of the new bonds.</p>
<p>The bonds, which will be dated and delivered on February 3, pay interest on June 1 and December 1, the government said.</p>
<p>Proceeds of the issue will be used for general purposes of the Government of Canada.</p>
<p>There are no Government of Canada marketable bonds maturing on February 3.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
